The surface a human or an agent drives: the `homma` binary and its command
families. `status`, `verify`, `repo`, `forge`, `org`, `agent`, `docs`, `migrate`
and `archive` read and move the workspace; `identity` renders and launches an
identity, matches an address to an agent and takes, renews and releases the lease
that lets one session at a time hold a name; `milestone` records each milestone with its freeze, head and tip, tells where
the current one began and reports on the range since; `search` asks one question of
every index the workspace holds, each hit naming its index; `summarise` reads a large text through one isolated
call of a small model and gives back a summary whose every line names its place; `ask` runs a
command and answers a question over its output through that pass, keeping what it paid for per
chunk; `release` gates a commit, records the
run, carries `dev` onto `main` as a tagged, published release, keeps the publish
credentials valid, and reports a repo's version timeline and the estate of
everything the workspace publishes.
